      <workList xml:id="workDesc_09212075">
         <work xml:id="work_id277f5d60">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_5db19c58">C1:009</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_idc75be445" xml:lang="de">Gültige Zeugnisse über die jüngste Matthesonisch-Musicalische Kern-Schrifft</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_37d7c69d">
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_d0f03d0c">Johann Mattheson</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="persName_id74e3f564">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_id0e8f69bf">
               <date isodate="1738" xml:id="date_f05e6266">1738</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_idde4540d9">
               <p xml:id="idm91">In 1737, <persName xml:id="idm92" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Mattheson</persName> published his <rend xml:id="idm93" fontstyle="italic">Kern melodischer Wißenschaft</rend> as a precurser of <rend xml:id="idm94" fontstyle="italic">Der </rend>
                  <rend xml:id="idm95" fontstyle="italic">Vollkommene Capellmeister</rend> which was to be one of his most popular and important music theoretical writings. <rend xml:id="idm96" fontstyle="italic">Kern melodischer Wißenschaft</rend> deals basically with the art of composition, that is, the musical styles and genres, melody, syntax and intervals. When dealing with the art of the fugue Mattheson criticises 'the artificial' ('der künstliche') style of <persName xml:id="idm97" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Sebastian Bach</persName>. In the beginning of 1738, Mattheson published the present supplement to <rend xml:id="idm98" fontstyle="italic">Kern melodischer Wißenschaft</rend> consisting of three letters of which the first two (one by 'C.H.P.' dated Oldenburg 24 October 1737; and the other by the organist <persName xml:id="idm99" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Paul Kunzten</persName>, dated 2 December 1737) are brief, and the third one which is by Scheibe and dated January 1738, is a detailed explication of the subject, in essence a recommendation of Mattheson’s work though he does have objections. At that time Scheibe was living in Hamburg and frequented the musical and intellectual circles which included among others Mattheson and <persName xml:id="idm100" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Georg Philipp Telemann</persName>. There is no doubt that many of the issues which Scheibe deals with in <rend xml:id="idm101" fontstyle="italic">Der Critische Musicus</rend> (1738–40; SchW C1:008) were inspired by Mattheson’s writings and the discussions which followed from their meetings.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_0fe62cf0">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="de">German</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="biblList_178N200E0">
               <head xml:id="head_f43ae63b">Bibliography</head>
               <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_b5632b5e">
                  <genre xml:id="genre_2c8e02db">book</genre>
                  <author xml:id="author_764f362a">Johann Adolph Scheibe</author>
                  <annot xml:id="annot_51948704">
                     <p xml:id="idm111">Scheibe mentions on sig. b7v: 'Ferner gefällt es dem Ungenannten, meine Abhandlung eine aristoxenische, mich aber einen Aristoxenus zu nennen; ungeachtet ich meine Schrift unter meinem eigenen Namen herausgegeben habe. Ich erinnere dieses aus der Ursache, weil es bekannt ist, daß Herr Mattheson sich des Namens Aristoxenus der jüngere schon mehr als einmal bedienet hat. Ich bin also nicht gesonnen, mich unter einer fremden Maske zu verbergen; zumal da sich bereits ein anderer dieselbe zugeeignet hat.'</p>
                  </annot>
                  <ptr label="Digitisation"
                       target="http://reader.digitale-sammlungen.de/de/fs1/object/display/bsb10599387_00036.html"
                       xml:id="ptr_6e8c6527"/>
                  <title level="m" xml:id="title_d1758bdd">Critischer Musikus</title>
                  <title level="s" xml:id="title_805145b2"/>
                  <biblScope xml:id="biblScope_b94a9be8">sig. b7v, p. 331</biblScope>
                  <imprint xml:id="imprint_fabde73c">
                     <date isodate="1745" xml:id="date_7a100893">1745</date>
                     <pubPlace xml:id="pubPlace_c453c3f0">Leipzig</pubPlace>
                  </imprint>
               </bibl>
            </biblList>
